.SH NAME
sm2file \- shared\-memory linked list data extraction test program
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
\&\fBsm2file\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
\&\fBsm2file\fR stress-tests shared-memory linked list data extraction by
retrieving and deleting all text file lines inserted into a shared-memory
linked list that is the root object of a PSM partition named "file2sm".
.PP
The operation of \fBsm2file\fR echoes the cyclical operation of \fBfile2sm\fR:
the EOF lines inserted into the linked list by \fBfile2sm\fR punctuate the
writing of files that are copies of \fBfile2sm\fR's original source text file.
The name of each file written by \fBsm2file\fR is file_copy_\fIcycleNbr\fR,
where \fIcycleNbr\fR is, in effect, the count of EOF lines encountered in the
linked list up to the point at which the writing of this file began.
.PP
\&\fBsm2file\fR may catch up with the data ingestion activity of \fBfile2sm\fR,
in which case it blocks (taking the \fBfile2sm\fR test semaphore) until
the linked list is no longer empty.
